---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="flexfetch: your whole system, fetched in milliseconds">
  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <header class="hero" id="top">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-split">
        <div class="hero-text reveal in d1">
          <h1>Your whole system.<br /><span class="accent">Fetched in milliseconds.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">
            flexfetch is a blazing-fast, themeable system info tool for Linux and macOS.
            Zero subprocesses, pure Rust.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-install">
            <div class="cmd-wrap">
              <code id="cmd-curl">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mahesh-diwan/flexfetch/main/install.sh | sh</code>
              <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="cmd-curl" aria-label="Copy command">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <div class="plat-hint" id="plat-hint"></div>
            <p class="install-note">Linux & macOS · checksum + signature verified</p>
          </div>

          <div class="hero-stats">
            <span class="hs"><strong>1.7 MB</strong> binary</span>
            <span class="hs-dot">·</span>
            <span class="hs"><strong>38</strong> modules</span>
            <span class="hs-dot">·</span>
            <span class="hs"><strong>527</strong> logos</span>
            <span class="hs-dot">·</span>
            <span class="hs rust-badge">Written in Rust</span>
          </div>
          <div class="social-proof">
            <span>MIT licensed</span>
            <span class="hs-dot">·</span>
            <span>contributions welcome</span>
            <span class="hs-dot">·</span>
            <a href="https://github.com/mahesh-diwan/flexfetch">star on GitHub</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-term reveal d2">
          <div class="term-bar">
            <span class="term-dot r" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="term-dot y" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="term-dot g" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="term-title">flexfetch</span>
          </div>
          <div class="term-body" id="hero-terminal">
            <div class="term-placeholder">Save your screenshot to public/terminal-shot.png</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ============ STATS ============ -->
  <section class="section stats" id="stats">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stats-row">
        <span class="stat-badge">38 modules</span>
        <span class="stat-badge">527 logos</span>
        <span class="stat-badge">0 subprocesses</span>
        <span class="stat-badge">1.7 MB</span>
        <span class="stat-badge rust">Rust</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FEATURES ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="features">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>Everything a fetch should be. Nothing it shouldn't.</h2>
        <p>Every module reads the system directly: <code>/proc</code>, sysfs, or macOS APIs. No subprocesses, no parsing, no startup cost.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bento-grid">
        <div class="feature-item reveal">
          <span class="feature-check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Zero subprocesses</h3>
            <p>Every collector reads kernel data directly. No forking, no parsing overhead. Warm runs complete in milliseconds.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item reveal d1">
          <span class="feature-check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Themes & gradients</h3>
            <p>Built-in presets (Catppuccin, Dracula, Nord, Solarized, Tokyo Night), truecolor everywhere, per-module key/value colors, gradient accents.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item reveal d2">
          <span class="feature-check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <div>
            <h3>ASCII & image logos</h3>
            <p>527 distro logos imported from fastfetch, plus PNG/BMP logos rendered as block characters with automatic palette extraction.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item reveal">
          <span class="feature-check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Live TUI dashboard</h3>
            <p><code>flexfetch --live</code> opens a TUI with CPU/memory/disk gauges, per-process bars, network sparklines.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item reveal d1">
          <span class="feature-check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Lua & WASM plugins</h3>
            <p>Write a custom module in Lua in five minutes, or ship memory-safe WebAssembly plugins that run with resource limits inside a sandbox.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item reveal d2">
          <span class="feature-check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Supply-chain hardened</h3>
            <p>Plugins install via a signed registry with checksum verification. Every entry is cryptographically verified before execution.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ INSTALL ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="install">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>On your machine in one command.</h2>
        <p>Releases ship Linux (musl static, 3 arches) and macOS (arm64 + x86_64) binaries. Every artifact includes checksums and signatures for verification.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="inst-grid">
        <div class="inst reveal">
          <div class="inst-head">
            <span class="badge">official</span>
            <h3>curl installer</h3>
            <p>Detects your platform, verifies the checksum before unpacking, and refuses to install anything if the file doesn't match.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="code-tabs">
              <span class="code-tab active">install</span>
            </div>
            <div class="code-body">
              <code id="cmd-curl2">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mahesh-diwan/flexfetch/main/install.sh | sh</code>
              <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="cmd-curl2" aria-label="Copy command">Copy</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="plat-hint" id="plat-hint2"></div>
          <div class="note">Linux & macOS · checksum + signature verified</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="secure-strip reveal">
        <span class="ok">✓ SHA-256 checksums</span>
        <span class="ok">✓ cosign signatures</span>
        <span class="ok">✓ supply-chain provenance</span>
        <span class="ok">✓ signed plugin registry</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    const heroTerm = document.getElementById("hero-terminal");
    if (heroTerm) {
      fetch("/flexfetch/terminal-shot.png", { method: "HEAD" })
        .then(r => {
          if (r.ok) {
            heroTerm.innerHTML = '<img src="/flexfetch/terminal-shot.png" alt="flexfetch terminal output" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;border-radius:0 0 7px 7px;" />';
          }
        })
        .catch(() => {});
    }
  </script>
  <style>
    .stats-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .stat-badge {
      font: 500 13px var(--font-mono);
      color: var(--muted);
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 8px 16px;
      transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
    }

    .stat-badge:hover {
      border-color: var(--border-strong);
    }

    .stat-badge.rust {
      color: var(--accent);
      border-color: rgba(232, 145, 58, 0.3);
      background: rgba(232, 145, 58, 0.06);
    }

    .code-block {
      background: #08090d;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .code-tabs {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 0 12px;
    }

    .code-tab {
      font: 500 11px var(--font-mono);
      color: var(--muted);
      padding: 10px 16px;
      border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
      cursor: default;
    }

    .code-tab.active {
      color: var(--text-strong);
      border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
    }

    .code-body {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 14px 16px;
    }

    .code-body code {
      font: 13px var(--font-mono);
      color: var(--accent);
      flex: 1;
      word-break: break-all;
    }

    .inst-head {
      padding: 0 0 16px 0;
    }

    .inst-head h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--text-strong);
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }

    .inst-head p {
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .hero-term {
      min-height: 380px;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .hero-term .term-body {
      flex: 1;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .hero-term .term-body img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1024px) {
      .hero-term {
        min-height: 280px;
        max-width: 540px;
        margin: 0 auto;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>